  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced Displacement and Mobility Tracking and Multi-Sectoral Support for Displaced Populations in Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The crisis in conflict-affected Northeast Nigeria remains one of the most severe in the world today, marked by armed conflict, forced displacement/returns and human rights and dignity violations. The impacts of the displacement crisis are diverse and complex, dislocating people from their homes, livelihoods and communities. In addition to insecurity, years 2021 and 2022 saw a rise in camp closures in Borno state, creating further hardships and risks for the affected population. This is further compounded by natural hazards which resulted in devastating floods leading to displacement and exacerbation of vulnerabilities. Through this Action, IOM aims to contribute towards strengthening the protection and resilience of crisis-affected populations. The provision of humanitarian assistance in the Northeast is highly dependent on trends and patterns of human mobility.</narrative>
  </description>
